<p>The United States said it revoked green cards or visas for several Iranian nationals tied to Iran’s current or former leadership, including Hamideh Soleimani Afshar, whom US officials identified as a niece of slain Iranian general Qassem Soleimani, and her daughter. The State Department said Secretary of State Marco Rubio determined this week that they were no longer eligible for lawful permanent resident status or entry to the US. Officials said ICE then took the two women into custody. US officials said the action also extended to other Iranian-linked individuals, including the daughter and son-in-law of Ali Larijani. The Trump administration said it would not let people it views as supporters of the Iranian government keep US immigration status.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/tTzhPFaU-AJH5lqSS1BAWue-ex_qFDKG6KdgSI3KIJNJ83zeLAAEfBfqyeg1DALH9zfToA1qTi7opnFw_OCZn08kl3Xch6upwwQ4C8w9-V_0' alt='An Iranian holds a picture of late General Qassem Soleimani as people gather to mourn him in Tehran, Iran on January 4, 2020.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Asylum history: CBS reported that Hamideh Soleimani Afshar and her daughter received US asylum in 2019 before the government moved to strip their green cards in 2026.</li><li>Broader scope: SCMP reported that the green-card or visa actions affected at least four Iranian nationals connected to Iran’s current or former government, not just the two women taken into custody.</li><li>Public rationale: The State Department cited press reports and Soleimani Afshar’s own social media posts as it described her as an outspoken supporter of Iran’s government.</li><li>Not all targets were in the US: Officials said the daughter and son-in-law of Ali Larijani were already outside the country and are barred from re-entering.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US State Department: The department said Secretary Rubio revoked the women’s status after deciding they were ineligible for lawful permanent residence or entry into the United States, framing the move as a legal eligibility decision. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-revokes-green-cards-and-visas-of-several-iranian-nationals-connected-to-tehran-government/article70824688.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Trump administration: Officials cast the move as part of a broader crackdown meant to stop people they see as supporters of Iran’s government from keeping US immigration benefits, presenting it as both immigration enforcement and a national-security measure. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/4/top-diplomat-marco-rubio-strips-qassem-soleimanis-niece-of-us-residency'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Soleimani family: NDTV reported that relatives denied Hamideh Soleimani Afshar was connected to Qassem Soleimani, disputing a central claim in the US account. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/us-iran-israel-war-qasem-soleimani-was-assassinated-in-2020-amid-iran-war-us-to-boot-his-niece-hamideh-soleimani-afshar-11311793#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-revokes-green-cards-and-visas-of-several-iranian-nationals-connected-to-tehran-government/article70824688.ece'>U.S. revokes green cards and visas of several Iranian nationals connected to Tehran government</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/4/top-diplomat-marco-rubio-strips-qassem-soleimanis-niece-of-us-residency'>Marco Rubio says he has stripped Qassem Soleimani’s niece of US residency</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/ex-iranian-guard-leader-soleimani-family-ice-custody/'>Family of Iran military leader Soleimani has U.S. residence visas revoked</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/inthenews/comments/1sco9c5/niece_grandniece_of_slain_iranian_gen_soleimani/'>Niece, grand-niece of slain Iranian Gen. Soleimani arrested by immigration agents</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='htt